[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The scene features two simple, matte white ceramic plates placed on an aged oak wood table, capturing a 3/4 overhead perspective at a 40-degree angle to showcase the texture of the pilaf. The primary plate is in sharp focus, while the second plate sits slightly behind and to the side, softly blurred. The pilaf consists of perfectly cooked brown rice grains with a distinct nutty texture, interspersed with bright, emerald-green wilted spinach. The spinach is tender and naturally wilted, not overcooked or mushy. Studded throughout are small, rustic chunks of toasted walnuts, providing golden-brown textural contrast. The rice is lightly tossed with shimmering extra-virgin olive oil, visible as subtle, reflective droplets catching the natural window light from the left. A faint dusting of cracked black pepper and finely grated lemon zest is visible on the surface. The scene is illuminated by soft, natural morning side light, creating gentle shadows and a warm, inviting atmosphere. Props include a rumpled linen napkin partially tucked under the main plate, a wooden spoon resting on the table next to the plate, and a few stray walnut fragments and a small garlic skin scattered near the rim. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The presentation is lived-in and authentic, with a small, natural sauce drip on the rim and an asymmetric distribution of ingredients, avoiding artificial symmetry. The overall tone is golden-hour warm, cozy, and professional editorial quality. No watermarks, no hands, no text, no synthetic plastic look."
]
